<title>INDIA: India M3 money supply drops to 16.1 pct on Feb 14.</title>
<headline>India M3 money supply drops to 16.1 pct on Feb 14.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's year-on-year M3 money supply growth was 16.1 percent on February 14, 1997, down from 16.2 percent on January 31, 1997, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.  </p>
<p>		   M3 MONEY SUPPLY GROWTH (yr-on-yr in pct)</p>
<p>		   Feb 14, 1997   Jan 31, 1997  Feb 2,1996</p>
<p>		   16.1	     16.2	    14.88</p>
<p>Money supply was 6,750.33 billion rupees on February 14, 1997 against 6,716.67 billion rupees on January 31, the RBI said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
